WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.200
I really hope Conis
is all right.

3
00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.610
You know she's gonna
have hell to pay

4
00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.200
when the White Berets
catch up with her

5
00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.780
and it's our own stupid fault.

6
00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:58.700
She'd be okay if she
hadn't helped us.

7
00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:00.860
And I'm not sure she can
trust that Sky Knight.

8
00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:02.670
He pretty much
gives me the creeps.

9
00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:04.070
He's kinda old and weird,

10
00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.020
but he doesn't seem like
that bad of a guy.

11
00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.480
There was no other choice.

12
00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.980
I wanna protect her,

13
00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:11.230
but it's not like we could've
brought her along with us.

14
00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:13.960
Man, this piece of junk is slow.

15
00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.500
Of course it is.

16
00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.790
It's gotta be several times
heavier than a standard waver.

17
00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.550
What'd you expect?

18
00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.580
<b>Adventure on God's Island</b>

19
00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:26.590
Uh, guys! Where did that
huge forest come from?

20
00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:28.140
Is that the Upper Yard?

21
00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:31.280
I don't remember
this being on the map.

22
00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:32.530
Wait.

23
00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:34.170
No, there is supposed
to be a forest ahead,

24
00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.830
but I don't see any warning
about how big it is.

25
00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:38.830
This cannot be right!

26
00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:40.920
Who knows how old that map is.

27
00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.130
We know it can be traced back
a couple hundred years,

28
00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:45.260
but who's to say it hasn't
been around longer?

29
00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.220
The forest may have been
a fraction of its size

30
00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:48.790
when that map was made.

31
00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.300
Ah, that's true.

32
00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:53.390
All I know is, I gotta
climb one of these trees!

33
00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:56.480
Ha! They're enormous!

34
00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:01.840
Look, the entrance!

35
00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.510
Well, this is it, Usopp.

36
00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:05.800
If you're gonna chicken out,
now's the time.

37
00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.010
Actually, if you don't mind,

38
00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:08.800
I was kind of thinking
I'd like to go back.

39
00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:09.800
Too late!

40
00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:11.430
Then why did you ask me?!

41
00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:36.890
Wh-What was that?

42
00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:38.430
Would you calm down?

43
00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:39.800
Yeah, take it easy.

44
00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:41.060
Open your eyes!

45
00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:43.140
Don't you notice
anything strange?

46
00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:44.900
Look at all these shipwrecks!

47
00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:46.310
It is a forest.

48
00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:47.360
He's right.

49
00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:48.570
That doesn't make any sense!

50
00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:50.400
Besides, they didn't
run aground...

51
00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:51.990
they were sliced in half!

52
00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:53.830
Did you hear that?

53
00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:56.070
The woods are full
of noises. Relax.

54
00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:56.790
I heard that.

55
00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:58.830
Full speed ahead!

56
00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.210
All ahead full!

57
00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:00.990
Stroke! Stroke!

58
00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:02.390
What's going on?

59
00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:05.250
Hm?

60
00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:10.120
A sickle monster!

61
00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:12.150
Hang on tight, here
comes another one!

62
00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.800
No. Not just one.

63
00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:22.900
Paddle like crazy!

64
00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:33.150
What the hell is this?!

65
00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.500
Watch where you're going!

66
00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:36.960
Luffy! No, wait! Slow down!

67
00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:39.620
This isn't working.
Usopp, take the wheel!

68
00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:40.950
Gum-Gum...

69
00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:42.540
What are you doing?
It's in front of us!

70
00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:44.250
I know, just hang on!

71
00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:46.940
...Bazooka!

72
00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:49.050
Ha-ha! Dodged it!

73
00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:51.590
Whoa! That was close!

74
00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:59.270
I think we finally outran it.

75
00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:00.980
Aw, but this is bad.

76
00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.530
Now it's too late to go back!

77
00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:05.530
Oh, I can't even see
the entrance anymore!

78
00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:06.780
Then stay here.

79
00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.450
I'd die, you idiot!

80
00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:09.780
More than likely

81
00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.920
Was that a big snake?

82
00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.670
Looked like a giant lamprey.

83
00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.670
A "Sky Lamprey" I guess.

84
00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:25.260
One that big will do more
than just suck a little blood.

85
00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:26.840
Neatest forest ever, huh?

86
00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:28.360
Neat forest my butt!

87
00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:31.120
If this is our so-called
ordeal, then I quit!

88
00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.660
You can't quit yet.
We just got here.

89
00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.500
We've got to keep moving.

90
00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:39.000
We can't spend any more time on
this Milky Road than necessary.

91
00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:42.250
Otherwise, we're asking
for certain death.

92
00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:50.710
There he is!

93
00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:51.630
Zoro!

94
00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:52.750
It's all my fault!

95
00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:54.960
What if he gets swallowed?

96
00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:04.960
Wait. Why hasn't
he come back up?

97
00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:08.340
Zoro, please be okay!

98
00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:11.130
You don't think he
got eaten, do you?

99
00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:14.180
Zoro's fish food!

100
00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:17.210
If he had been eaten, the clouds
would've turned red by now.

101
00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:20.270
How can you stay so
calm at a time like this?

102
00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:22.680
I am so done with you!

103
00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:42.370
[ZORO
I can tell you one thing.

104
00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:46.040
We are not gonna make
it across by swimming.

105
00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:48.160
What kinda swordsman
punches a shark

106
00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:49.290
'stead of usin' his blade?

107
00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:50.960
I'm so glad you're okay!

108
00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:53.200
One thing's for certain,

109
00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:56.740
we're definitely somewhere
in the middle of Upper Yard.

110
00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:58.080
Hmm.

111
00:06:58.160 --> 00:06:59.720
This seems to be some sort
of altar for sacrifices.

112
00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:01.180
Uh. Hey, look!

113
00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:04.090
There's a giant head
blocking our way!

114
00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:07.850
Not quite. It's a statue.

115
00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:11.200
Oh, right. But it looks
like a total dead end.

116
00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.200
No, look, there's
four entrances.

117
00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:16.360
Of course.

118
00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:17.900
And how much you wanna
bet all four of 'em

119
00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:20.240
lead to different places?

120
00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:23.330
Ordeal of Swamp, Ordeal of Iron,

121
00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:27.120
Ordeal of String,
and Ordeal of Spheres.

122
00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:29.750
Ha-ha! You think we
get to take our pick?

123
00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:31.460
Is it me, or do none
of these things

124
00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:34.500
really sound like much
of an "ordeal"?

125
00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:40.880
Uh. I don't know, guys.

126
00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.930
Which one should we choose?

127
00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:46.980
Prepare for judgment, criminals.

128
00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:49.730
You have no choice
but to receive it.

129
00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:54.940
Select a gate.
Select from four ordeals.

130
00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:59.280
For you, there can be
no turning back.

131
00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:05.080
You may choose your own trial,
but we will decide your fate.

132
00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:07.470
Swamp!

133
00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:10.730
Iron!

134
00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.300
String!

135
00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:15.050
Spheres!

136
00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:20.560
– Choose your path, criminals!
– Choose your path, criminals!

137
00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:22.860
So what do we do?

138
00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:25.190
Um, let's go with spheres.

139
00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:26.320
Why do you like that one?

140
00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:27.900
Spheres are like balls, right?

141
00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:28.680
Sounds fun.

142
00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:29.860
That's your only reason?

143
00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:32.320
They're ordeals, they're
not supposed to be fun!

144
00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.400
Not that I'm
disagreeing with you.

145
00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:38.280
Spheres is definitely the one
that doesn't sound too violent.

146
00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:39.820
At least to me.

147
00:08:39.820 --> 00:08:42.690
Then it's decided. Just don't
let your guard down, guys.

148
00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:44.570
Remember, these
are God's Islands,

149
00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:48.320
10,000 meters above sea level...
anything can happen.

150
00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:50.580
Ready! Let's do this!

151
00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:04.220
Driver, would you mind
not shutting your eyes?

152
00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:08.550
No. It's just as
dark with them open.

153
00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:11.090
Hey, guys, what if this
is like one of those games?

154
00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:12.350
Like a what?

155
00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:13.470
You know,
if you pick the right door

156
00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:14.930
then you get a prize.

157
00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:16.410
But if you pick the wrong one...

158
00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:19.000
What are you talking about?
What if we picked wrong?

159
00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:21.710
Why couldn't you have
mentioned this before, Luffy?

160
00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:23.830
Well, let's see here. Um...

161
00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:27.920
If you pick the wrong one...
then you fall off the island!

162
00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.340
How can you say
something so stupid?!

163
00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:33.180
We're thousands of
meters in the air!

164
00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:34.710
I don't know how
many times your life

165
00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:36.960
can flash before your eyes
during a fall like that,

166
00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:38.710
and I don't wanna know!

167
00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:41.220
You guys are both being idiots.

168
00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:43.340
Nothing like that's gonna...

169
00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:06.120
You've gotta be kidding me!

170
00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:25.180
Ah! There's an
entire school of 'em!

171
00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:26.970
What are we gonna do?

172
00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.230
I'm not sure.

173
00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:30.140
But if that first one
was any indication,

174
00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:32.650
we're not gonna have much
luck fightin' 'em off.

175
00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:34.230
We've got to do something.

176
00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.230
We can't stay here forever.

177
00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:40.570
If leaving us here was that
lobster's idea of a joke,

178
00:10:40.650 --> 00:10:42.700
it's not very funny.

179
00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:44.580
Perhaps this is the
"Heaven's Judgment"

180
00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:46.610
we've been hearing
so much about.

181
00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:48.530
'Cept you'd think this
"God" would try something

182
00:10:48.610 --> 00:10:49.950
a little flashier, ya know?

183
00:10:50.030 --> 00:10:54.080
Eh. Couldn't say,
never met the guy.

184
00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:56.290
I'm not sure
what the solution is.

185
00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:59.670
We definitely can't set sail
with the hull looking like this.

186
00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:02.330
Hey, Chopper, try to figure
out a way to fix the ship.

187
00:11:02.420 --> 00:11:04.460
Uh, me? Okay!

188
00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:07.570
Why should he fix it?
Are you going somewhere?

189
00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:09.910
I'm gonna find
a way into the forest.

190
00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:12.620
We should probably make
this our base of operations.

191
00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:13.990
You guys can keep a lookout.

192
00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:17.310
I'm sure Luffy and the others
are headed this way.

193
00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:18.900
Like they say,
if you get lost,

194
00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:20.730
you should stay
where you are, right?

195
00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:23.160
Shouldn't that
apply to you, too?

196
00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:26.420
Hm.

197
00:11:33.260 --> 00:11:35.760
Zoro, if you wanna
go into the forest,

198
00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:37.480
well, I guess that's
okay with me.

199
00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:39.650
But you haven't really
told us what for.

200
00:11:39.770 --> 00:11:42.020
There's supposed to be some
kinda God on this island...

201
00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:43.120
I wanna meet him.

202
00:11:43.190 --> 00:11:45.320
Wait. That's a terrible idea!

203
00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:48.590
I mean, what are you gonna do
when you actually find him?

204
00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:52.000
I don't know. Depends on
if he behaves himself.

205
00:11:52.090 --> 00:11:55.090
Zoro, you're the
bravest person I know.

206
00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:57.680
And what about his priests,
you gonna beat them up, too?

207
00:11:57.760 --> 00:12:00.640
Hello? The last thing we need
is you pissing off a God!

208
00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:02.600
It's kinda not smart!

209
00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:07.880
By the time I'm done with him...

210
00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:10.220
...this "God" is gonna
bow before me.

211
00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:12.020
Ah-ha! Go, Zoro!

212
00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:13.730
I don't believe in him anyway.

213
00:12:16.140 --> 00:12:17.850
What do I care about
pissing him off?

214
00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:21.400
O powerful one,
I just wanted you to know

215
00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:23.650
I don't agree with
my idiot shipmate.

216
00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:25.400
I don't even like him that much.

217
00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:26.820
Okay, bye.

218
00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:31.850
That vine looks pretty sturdy.

219
00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:34.670
Ah. Excellent idea.

220
00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:36.970
Mind if I tag along, swordsman?

221
00:12:37.050 --> 00:12:40.050
Sure. Long as you
promise not to slow me down.

222
00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:43.140
Wait a minute!
Where do you think you're going?

223
00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:45.570
Look at this.

224
00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:47.360
At least a thousand
years have passed

225
00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:49.220
since this altar was built.

226
00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:51.360
– A thousand years?
– A thousand years?

227
00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:53.950
The sense of history
here is amazing.

228
00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:57.410
It gives me chills. You feel it?

229
00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:59.370
– Uhh...
– Uhh...

230
00:12:59.470 --> 00:13:01.760
A place as ancient
as this is sure to be filled

231
00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:05.100
with all kinds of old relics.

232
00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:07.600
Imagine all the valuables
we could discover.

233
00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:09.840
Just think: The
possibilities are endless.

234
00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:11.100
Hm.

235
00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:12.560
In that case, I'll join you.

236
00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:15.560
Nami! I thought you
were too scared!

237
00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:17.900
It's for history.

238
00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:19.820
Yeah, sure it is.

239
00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:25.200
That work for ya?

240
00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:36.690
It's official.
He's lost his mind.

241
00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:48.200
She made it!

242
00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:49.960
Looks easy enough.

243
00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:56.090
This is higher up
than I thought.

244
00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:57.380
Be careful.

245
00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:59.670
If you fall, you'll
most certainly die.

246
00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:02.400
That supposed to
be your idea of helping?!

247
00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:08.120
Whoa. She's right.

248
00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:10.330
I'm dead if I fall.

249
00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:12.120
Nami?

250
00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:21.140
Help me! It's too fast!
I'm gonna crash!

251
00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:26.730
Look at that,
you're not gutless.

252
00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:30.900
Thanks for catching me.

253
00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:31.900
Anytime.

254
00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:33.590
...is what you should've done.

255
00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:37.370
That had nothing to do with it!

256
00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:42.250
This forest is even
bigger than I thought.

257
00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:46.470
Okay, Chopper! You're
in charge of the ship!

258
00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:47.720
We're counting on you!

259
00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:49.180
We'll be back soon!

260
00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:52.060
Bye! Everyone be careful!

261
00:14:52.150 --> 00:14:54.440
Don't take too long, okay?

262
00:14:57.390 --> 00:15:00.460
I guess Nami will be all right
since she's with Robin and Zoro.

263
00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:04.530
My friends are all so
brave and adventurous.

264
00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:07.280
I'm too scared to go,
but maybe someday,

265
00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:10.740
if I'm really lucky,
I can be brave like them, too.

266
00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:12.080
Oh, well. If I can't be brave,

267
00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:14.790
I can at least
make myself useful.

268
00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:17.080
Being left alone in the middle
of a dangerous forest

269
00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:19.460
to fix our ship is proof that
everyone must trust me,

270
00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:22.290
so I have to do my very best.

271
00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:26.130
It's just little old me, all by
myself in the big scary forest.

272
00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:31.900
Oh, no! Who's gonna protect me?

273
00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:36.750
We're alive?

274
00:15:37.590 --> 00:15:39.340
I seriously thought
we were falling

275
00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:41.090
all the way back
to the Blue Sea.

276
00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:44.760
That's because somebody
had to make up

277
00:15:44.850 --> 00:15:46.890
a lame story to scare us!

278
00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:49.340
I was scared! I thought
I was a goner, too!

279
00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:57.310
All right, so what
is this place?

280
00:15:57.540 --> 00:16:00.210
A forest. With balls.

281
00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:09.590
They're balls
made of Island Cloud.

282
00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:11.220
Ha! Awesome!

283
00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:13.430
They look like really
big snowflakes.

284
00:16:13.510 --> 00:16:15.260
Now what could be
scary about that?

285
00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:17.380
See, Usopp? It's okay.

286
00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:22.420
Heads up, the Milky Road is
leading us up into the trees.

287
00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:25.320
I just don't see how this
is an ordeal. Do you?

288
00:16:26.030 --> 00:16:27.700
Not yet.

289
00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:29.410
It'd be great if there
was nothing ahead,

290
00:16:29.490 --> 00:16:31.490
but somehow I doubt it.

291
00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:33.240
What if it was
like one of those games,

292
00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:34.450
and we picked the right door,

293
00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:36.040
and now all we have
to do is float around

294
00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:38.540
in this giant snow
looking for the others?

295
00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:42.890
Y-Y-Yeah! M-Maybe that's it!

296
00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:44.180
You're still being idiots.

297
00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:45.350
They think we're criminals,

298
00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:47.800
I doubt they'll let
us off that easy.

299
00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:49.970
Use your brains for once.

300
00:16:50.050 --> 00:16:51.220
I wouldn't be surprised

301
00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:53.850
if there were more traps
like the ones earlier.

302
00:16:53.930 --> 00:16:55.850
We have to stay sharp.

303
00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:59.000
Let's just keep moving.

304
00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:00.600
What, are you the captain now?

305
00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:01.940
Can we at least have a snack?

306
00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:05.350
Ooh! Yeah!
Whatcha got in your bag, Sanji?

307
00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:06.570
Come on, gimme!

308
00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:08.060
No! No snacks!

309
00:17:08.070 --> 00:17:10.160
But, Sanji, we need
to keep our strength up!

310
00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:11.280
Just a little somethin'?

311
00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:12.830
I said no!

312
00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:15.210
Now listen, it's really simple:
I'm going to keep steering,

313
00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:17.330
you guys keep watch
out the sides.

314
00:17:21.670 --> 00:17:25.970
Whoa. I didn't realize how
high up we were getting!

315
00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:27.740
Something's not right.

316
00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:29.260
It's too quiet.

317
00:17:29.350 --> 00:17:30.510
There are four priests,

318
00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:32.770
so I assumed each
tunnel would lead to one.

319
00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:35.550
Why haven't we seen
any of them yet?

320
00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:37.460
I got a bad feeling about this.

321
00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:39.970
Hey, Usopp! Catch!

322
00:17:40.050 --> 00:17:43.050
Okay, I got it,
I got it. Pass!

323
00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:45.170
I thought I told you
to keep watch!

324
00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:50.640
A snake!

325
00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:53.610
Stupid... snake ball!

326
00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:01.680
Okay, didn't see that coming.

327
00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:04.680
Ah! Sanji! Cloud ball!

328
00:18:04.760 --> 00:18:06.180
Kick it away!

329
00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:09.810
I do not like the idea of
being surrounded by snake eggs.

330
00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:29.460
– This can't be good.
– This can't be good.

331
00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:34.060
For cryin' out loud!
What's with these things?

332
00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:41.610
Silly children,
these are Surprise Clouds.

333
00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:46.760
You never know what's
going to come out of them.

334
00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:49.010
Hey? Where's that
voice coming from?

335
00:18:49.090 --> 00:18:51.260
Ha-ha! Heso!

336
00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:52.550
Who...?

337
00:18:54.390 --> 00:18:56.310
I'm so glad you picked
my challenge...

338
00:18:55.570 --> 00:19:00.490
<b>Satori of the Forest
Skypiea Priest</b>

339
00:18:56.390 --> 00:18:58.310
the Ordeal of Spheres!

340
00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:00.720
Yeah, is that
a talking dumpling?

341
00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:12.510
This guy is one of
Eneru's priests?

342
00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:17.180
That's the ordeal? Ball guy?

343
00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:20.640
Stop with the dancing!
And tell us who you are!

344
00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:26.730
Gotta say, he's not as
bright as I expected.

345
00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:29.390
Didn't Nami and the old guy
say these priests were strong?

346
00:19:29.470 --> 00:19:30.800
'Cause I'm not seein' it.

347
00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:35.510
Hey! Dumpling!

348
00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:38.230
Nami and the others
better be safe!

349
00:19:38.380 --> 00:19:39.700
The sacrifices?

350
00:19:39.930 --> 00:19:42.890
They'll escape or they won't.
Doesn't really matter which.

351
00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:44.390
If they escape, they'll die.

352
00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:47.560
If they're sacrificed,
well, they'll die then, too.

353
00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:49.020
What's that mean?

354
00:19:49.110 --> 00:19:51.110
But I'd be more
worried about yourselves.

355
00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:53.800
You'll have to beat me if you
plan on going any further.

356
00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.880
And I really don't see
that happening.

357
00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:02.060
He's comin' right for
us, Luffy! Get him!

358
00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:04.430
I hope you're ready for this!

359
00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:06.140
Gum-Gum...

360
00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:08.770
Ooh! You gonna stretch?

361
00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:13.360
...Pistol!

362
00:20:18.540 --> 00:20:19.290
No way!

363
00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:30.000
Luffy!

364
00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:42.130
Luffy!

365
00:20:42.210 --> 00:20:43.800
You're okay, aren't you?

366
00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:46.470
A hit like that couldn't
have hurt you that much!

367
00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:47.680
Well, you see,

368
00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:51.930
it's not what you'd
call a... normal hit.

369
00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:53.890
I'll show you not normal!

370
00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:56.110
Right foot, high kick.

371
00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:58.010
Boulette... Uh.

372
00:20:58.070 --> 00:20:59.950
Only the most well-trained

373
00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:02.120
are granted the power of...

374
00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:03.620
..."Mantra."

375
00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:04.910
Impossible!

376
00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:06.910
How could he have
predicted my attack?

377
00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:08.920
Ah!

378
00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:21.220
No! Sanji!

379
00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:23.990
I warned you, didn't I?

380
00:21:24.070 --> 00:21:25.490
Impact!

381
00:21:28.650 --> 00:21:31.600
The shock destroys the
body from the inside out.

382
00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:40.800
Sanji. Usopp.

383
00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:43.880
Yeah, I'm fine.

384
00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:47.090
Ugh. What did that
bastard do to us?

385
00:21:47.180 --> 00:21:48.760
I got no idea.

386
00:21:48.840 --> 00:21:50.470
Who is this guy anyway?

387
00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:52.910
My name is Satori.

388
00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:55.670
I am one of the four priests
of the almighty Eneru,

389
00:21:55.720 --> 00:21:57.060
who watch over Upper Yard

390
00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:59.660
and see to the judgment of
criminals like yourselves.

391
00:21:59.740 --> 00:22:02.460
I own the vearth
in this Lost Forest.

392
00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:04.200
The Lost Forest?

393
00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:06.180
Why, yes.

394
00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:10.020
My forest, in all its glory.

395
00:22:10.100 --> 00:22:11.640
And now...

396
00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:16.820
...your boat will be
lost in its illusions!

397
00:22:16.970 --> 00:22:19.760
Ah! We're using that!

398
00:22:19.820 --> 00:22:22.820
She will now speed
along the Milky Road,

399
00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:26.990
eventually weaving her way
to this forest's only exit!

400
00:22:27.070 --> 00:22:29.570
I'm sure I don't
need to tell you this,

401
00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:32.080
but if you lose a
dial boat in here,

402
00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:37.290
it's the same as losing your
way to the sacrificial altar.

403
00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:39.250
That means you will
have to find the boat

404
00:22:39.340 --> 00:22:41.340
and board her
before that happens.

405
00:22:41.420 --> 00:22:44.170
Of course, my hundreds
of Surprise Clouds and I

406
00:22:44.270 --> 00:22:47.640
will never allow
you that chance.

407
00:22:47.730 --> 00:22:50.440
Does that seem unfair
to you boys?

408
00:22:50.540 --> 00:22:52.500
Welcome to the Upper Yard!

409
00:22:57.250 --> 00:22:58.960
The Ordeal of Spheres.

410
00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:02.630
There's a ten percent
survival rate, so good luck.

411
00:23:02.710 --> 00:23:07.010
Survival rate. Just ten percent?
